Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates hands-on design of a real-time RAG system, including multi-embedding chunking, multi-stage retrieval, and data freshness in production-like conditions.

Key Concepts
- Dual-embedding chunking
- Vector DB indexing and cosine search
- Cross-encoder reranking
- Streaming updates and TTL pruning
- Latency targets and observability

Code Example
```javascript
async function retrieve(query) {
  const eSent = await embed(query, 'sentence');
  const eSect = await embed(query, 'section');
  const topSent = vectorDB.search(eSent,  topK);
  const topSect = vectorDB.search(eSect, topK);
  // fuse and rerank
  return rerank(topSent, topSect, query);
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure and improve retrieval quality in production?
- How would your design adapt if the vector DB spans multiple regions with different latencies?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a candidate’s ability to design end-to-end evaluation for private, privacy-conscious enterprise assistants, focusing on faithfulness, hallucination, and safety under real-world data/versioning constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Grounding to versioned sources and source IDs
- Hallucination detection in live responses
- Privacy safety: PII/secret leakage checks in output and citations
- Performance metrics under load and latency budgets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal evaluation script outline (pseudo)
function evaluate(model, corpus) {
  const prompts = loadPrompts();
  return prompts.map(p => {
    const out = model.respond(p);
    const grounded = ground(out, corpus, p);
    return { prompt: p, output: out, grounded };
  });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you detect partial grounding failures (e.g., only some claims anchored)?
- How would you integrate this into a CI/CD pipeline with private data access controls?
